ush possibility\n\nReason:\nI should bet for value here. My straight is strong, and the opponent's passive play (checking the turn) suggests they don't have a flush. A medium-sized bet of around 800-1000 chips will extract value from hands like two pair, trips, or a weaker straight while not overcommitting if they somehow have a flush or full house. Given that I'm already winning overall and want to maintain my lead, a modest value bet is optimal.\n\nAnswer: 800"}
